Project: NEO Arcana, a static one-page tarot-style team site (Vite + vanilla JS + plain CSS + GSAP).

Sources of truth, read before changing anything:
- CURSOR_PROMPT.md: full build spec and milestones.
- DESIGN.md: short design reference (colors, fonts, shape, motion, accessibility).
- src/data/team.json: all content.

Rules:
- Use colors only through CSS variables from src/styles/tokens.css. Never hardcode colors.
- The per-member `--card-accent` is only for card glow and small profile details, never for UI chrome.
- Fonts: Philosopher for headings, Lora for body. Both self-hosted via @fontsource with the cyrillic and latin subsets.
- Animate only transform and opacity with GSAP. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- UI text is Ukrainian. Code, comments and commit messages are English.
- Allowed runtime libraries are exactly gsap and lenis (Lenis only for desktop fine-pointer wheel smoothing, off on touch and prefers-reduced-motion); no others without approval. No localStorage, no features that are not in CURSOR_PROMPT.md.
- Work one milestone at a time. After a milestone, stop and tell me how to run it and what to check.
- If a file from the spec is missing (logo SVG, team.json, a placeholder image), create it following the spec instead of asking.
- vite.config.js must keep `base: './'`.
- Keep each source file focused and under about 250 lines. Keep the browser console free of errors and warnings.
- For a bug fix or small tweak, change only what was asked. No refactoring on the side.
